::GEO_U02_L07_GP_Q01::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L07_GP_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.TRI.1<br><br>Question:<br>Two sides and the included angle are marked congruent in two triangles. Which criterion applies? {
~ SSA#This choice reflects a misconception: SSA. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
= SAS#Correct. SAS matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ AAA#This choice reflects a misconception: AAA. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ HL#This choice reflects a misconception: HL. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

::GEO_U02_L07_GP_Q02::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L07_GP_Q02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.6<br><br>Question:<br>A rotation maps triangle ABC exactly onto triangle DEF. What congruence conclusion is supported? {
~ ABC is larger than DEF#This choice reflects a misconception: ABC is larger than DEF. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ ABC is similar but not congruent to DEF#This choice reflects a misconception: ABC is similar but not congruent to DEF. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
= Triangle ABC &cong; triangle DEF#Correct. Triangle ABC &cong; triangle DEF matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ No conclusion is possible#This choice reflects a misconception: No conclusion is possible. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

::GEO_U02_L07_GP_Q03::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L07_GP_Q03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.TRI.3<br><br>Question:<br>Why does a valid triangle congruence criterion support a rigid-motion explanation? {
= It gives enough evidence for one triangle to match the other#Correct. It gives enough evidence for one triangle to match the other matches the evidence and the MLA standard for this item.
~ It changes side lengths#This choice reflects a misconception: It changes side lengths. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ It proves only similarity#This choice reflects a misconception: It proves only similarity. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
~ It ignores corresponding parts#This choice reflects a misconception: It ignores corresponding parts. Recheck the evidence and apply the lesson concept before choosing.
}

